B.aaL=new A.LH("Terms & Conditions","By using HomeSplit you agree to these simple terms.\n\nTHE SERVICE\nHomeSplit helps a household record shared expenses, split them exactly, verify receipts and settle balances between members. It is a record-keeping tool: it does not hold, transfer or guarantee money between users.\n\nACCURACY\nMembers are responsible for the expenses and receipts they enter. Verification and dispute tools are provided so roommates can check each other's entries; HomeSplit is not responsible for disagreements between household members.\n\nACCOUNTS\nKeep your PIN private. A 4-digit PIN is a convenience lock, not a bank-grade credential - protect your device with its own lock screen as well. You are responsible for activity under your account.\n\nACCEPTABLE USE\nDo not enter other people's personal or payment details without their consent, and do not use the app for unlawful purposes.\n\nAVAILABILITY\nThe app is provided as-is for the RC3 demonstration. Features may change as the project develops.",null)
B.aaM=new A.LH("Privacy Policy","HomeSplit is a shared-living expense app. This policy explains what the app stores and why.\n\nWHAT WE STORE\n- Your account: name, email address, a securely hashed PIN (never the PIN itself), and your profile photo if you add one.\n- Your household data on this device: expenses, receipts you attach, shopping lists, payment account details you enter, payment requests, settlements and notifications.\n- If the backend is connected, account records are stored on that server so you can sign in.\n\nWHAT WE NEVER DO\n- We never store your Google password. Google sign-in happens on Google's own pages and we only receive a verified identity token.\n- We never sell your data or use it for advertising.\n- Demo Mode data never leaves your device and is never mixed with a real account.\n\nPAYMENTS\nHomeSplit records who owes whom; it does not move money. JazzCash, Easypaisa and bank details you save are shown to your household members so they can pay you directly in their own banking apps.\n\nYOUR CONTROL\nYou can download your data, change your PIN, revoke other sessions, or delete your account at any time from Settings. Deleting your account removes your account record; shared household records kept by other members on their devices are theirs to manage.\n\nThis policy ships with the app for the RC3 demonstration deployment. For a public release, publish this text at a stable URL and link it here.",null)
